.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Ascon-XOF128 extendable-output function\&. 

An extendable-output function (XOF) generalises a hash function by allowing the caller to request a digest of any desired byte length rather than a fixed-size output\&. ASCON-XOF128 realises this construction through a sponge operating over a 320-bit permutation state, absorbing the padded message in 64-bit rate blocks and squeezing an arbitrary number of output bytes through repeated applications of the Ascon-p permutation, as standardised in NIST SP 800-232\&.

.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
https://doi.org/10.6028/NIST.SP.800-232
.RE
