.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "void VERUM_ASCON_XOF128_digest (uint8_t * message, uint32_t message_size, uint8_t * digest, uint32_t digest_size)"

.PP
Ascon-XOF128 extendable-output digest\&. Computes \fRdigest_size\fP bytes of output from \fRmessage\fP using the Ascon-XOF128 sponge construction defined in Algorithm 9 of NIST SP 800-232 Section 5\&.2\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fImessage\fP Input message buffer\&. May be \fRNULL\fP if and only if \fRmessage_size\fP is zero, in which case the XOF output over the empty string is produced\&. 
.br
\fImessage_size\fP Byte length of \fRmessage\fP\&. May be zero\&. 
.br
\fIdigest\fP Destination buffer for the output digest\&. The caller is responsible for providing a buffer of at least \fRdigest_size\fP bytes\&. 
.br
\fIdigest_size\fP Desired output length in bytes\&. Must be greater than zero\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBPrecondition\fP
.RS 4
\fRdigest\fP is non-NULL\&. 

.PP
\fRmessage\fP is non-NULL when \fRmessage_size\fP is greater than zero\&. 

.PP
\fRmessage\fP points to a readable buffer of at least \fRmessage_size\fP bytes\&. 

.PP
\fRdigest\fP points to a writable buffer of at least \fRdigest_size\fP bytes\&. 

.PP
\fRdigest_size\fP is greater than zero\&. 

.PP
\fRmessage\fP and \fRdigest\fP do not overlap\&. 
.RE
.PP

